The linker error `undefined reference to '__device_dts_ord_32'` originates from `drivers/i2c/i2c_emul.c` at the line where `DT_FOREACH_CHILD_STATUS_OKAY` is used to iterate over children of an I2C emulation controller. The `EMUL_LINK_AND_COMMA` macro within this loop calls `DEVICE_DT_GET(node_id)`.

This error typically occurs when a device node is defined in the Device Tree (DTS) but lacks a `compatible` property, or its `compatible` property refers to a driver that is not enabled or linked. In such cases, the Zephyr build system cannot generate the necessary device object, leading to an undefined reference during linking.

Looking at `tests/drivers/fuel_gauge/sy24561/boards/native_sim.overlay`:
```dts
&i2c0 {
	sy24651: sy24651@48 {
		reg = <0x48>;
		status = "okay";
	};
};
```
The `sy24651@48` node is missing the `compatible` property. This is the direct cause of the linker error, as `DEVICE_DT_GET` for this node cannot resolve to any driver.

The test `tests/drivers/fuel_gauge/sy24561/src/test_sy24561.c` uses `DEVICE_DT_GET_ANY(silergy_sy24561)`, indicating that it expects a device with `compatible = "silergy,sy24561"`. The `native_sim_64.overlay` correctly includes this `compatible` property.

To fix the linker error in `native_sim.overlay`, the `compatible` property must be added to the `sy24651@48` node, matching the expected device type.

```
tests/drivers/fuel_gauge/sy24561/boards/native_sim.overlay
<<<<<<<< SEARCH
&i2c0 {
	sy24651: sy24651@48 {
		reg = <0x48>;
		status = "okay";
	};
};
========
&i2c0 {
	sy24651: sy24651@48 {
		compatible = "silergy,sy24561";
		reg = <0x48>;
		status = "okay";
	};
};
>>>>>>>> REPLACE
```
